A||||6||DavidHenshaw||Engine conversion ||||1||
Z||000000||DavidHenshaw||12-28-2000||04:16 PM||||With the variety of approaches to engine conversion for the Fiero it seems logical that someone would write a piece on the subject. In my mind this would not be a detailed treatment but would give enough information for someone to decide which engine they wanted to consider for their particular needs. <P>If this hasn't been done already I invite anyone interested to start by listing the engines they are aware have been used to date.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula 18||12-28-2000||06:24 PM||||IDK of any such article but would like to read one. I have an article here the compare three engines but there are lots they left out. <P>Possible engine conversions: <BR>I am gonna try and go by displacement<BR>2.0L Turbo 88-90 ?<BR>2.4L QuadFour 88-94<BR>SuperDuty4 many versions<BR>3.1L ??<BR>3.4L pushrod 91-95<BR>3.4L TDC ??<BR>3.5L "ShortStar"<BR>3.8L 86-91<BR>3800 Series I 91-95<BR>3800 Series I SC 91-93, 94-95<BR>3800 Series II 95 up<BR>3800 Series II SC 95 up<BR>4.1L,4.5L,4.9L Caddys<BR>4.3L Chevy 90* v6<BR>5.7L SBC<P>DID I miss any? <P>Basically if you can think about it you can swap it in there <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||12-28-2000||06:32 PM||||The regular northstar, unless that is one of the caddy engines. 3.1 Is also the easiest as I understand.||||reg||1
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||12-28-2000||07:06 PM||||has anyone sucessfully installed a shortstar?<BR>seems like it would be a good one to do but the engines not readily available yet since its only a couple years old.<BR>just random thoughts.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE  88FORMULA<BR>KissMySSFiero@netzero.net<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">  <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"||||reg||1
