Z||000005||hugh||12-28-2000||07:26 PM||||If the drivetrain would stand up to the torque generated by a 3.8 GN engine mounted transversely,you would have a vehicle capable of doing wheelstands and getting well over 20 miles a gallon.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||12-28-2000||08:06 PM||||hugh, if i got a fiero that already had no trunk (looks like i will) dose your north-south configuration look like it could be any easier to do than a tranverse install? it seems the main shortcoming of a longitudnal enginge is losing the trunk, so without that worry i want to gather some info on it. do you have an address (email or otherwise) for that guy who wrote that book on how its done?||||reg||1
